---
scope: src/app/learn/mcp-server-for-development-workflow
alignment: unreviewed
description: The /learn install quickstart for people searching 'mcp server for development workflow', covering what the aidemd MCP server adds, the real install, the first run and its tools.
intent: >
  This page answers people searching 'mcp server for development workflow'
  with an install quickstart. It opens with one paragraph on what
  @aidemd-mcp/server is and what an MCP server adds to a development workflow,
  then gives the real install command with a copy button and says what that
  command sets up. It walks the first run of /aide, names the tools the server
  exposes with a link to the Tools docs, and lists only the clients the package
  supports. Nothing on the page is invented. Readers leave installed, with links
  on to the Claude Code subagents pipeline page and the docs.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - The page opens with one paragraph saying what the aidemd MCP server is and what an MCP server adds to a development workflow, before any section.
    - The page shows the one real install command with a copy button, and says what running it sets up in the reader's project.
    - The page walks the first run of /aide after install, so a reader knows what to type and what happens next.
    - The page names the tools the server exposes and links to the Tools docs for the detail of each.
    - Supported clients appear only as the package actually supports them.
    - The page links on to the Claude Code subagents pipeline page and the docs.
  undesired:
    - An install command, flag or step the package does not have, or a shown command that differs from what the copy button copies.
    - A client named as supported, or given setup steps, that the package does not support.
    - A tool list that names a tool the server does not expose or disagrees with the Tools docs.
    - A first run described with prompts, output or results that /aide does not actually produce.
    - An opening that defines or pitches intent-driven engineering at length before saying what the server is and how to install it, work that belongs to the definition page.
    - A walkthrough of the full spec-to-QA pipeline in place of the first run, work that belongs to the subagents pipeline page.
---
